{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-4989-r4518589","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Chickpea Curry (Masaledaar Chole)","sourcePageId":4989,"sourceRevision":"4518589","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:30:54Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Chickpea%20Curry%20(Masaledaar%20Chole)&oldid=4518589","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:35:27.604Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Gluten-free recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Low-GI recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes for stew","Category:Recipes using chickpea","Category:Recipes using cilantro","Category:Recipes using curry powder","Category:Recipes using garam masala","Category:Recipes using garlic paste","Category:Recipes using ginger paste","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Vegan recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"b20e601ea992e0a7bb827fda38ff6540862be1651f9664d5b7ad532f98511742","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Curry recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Indian cuisine]]\n\n'''Masaladaar chole''' is a dish of chickpeas in spicy gravy.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] dried [[Cookbook:Chickpea|chickpeas]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] cooking [[Cookbook:Oil|oil]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]], medium chopped\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Chili Powder|chilli powder]]\n*1½ teaspoon Madras [[Cookbook:Curry Powder|curry powder]]\n*¼ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Garam Masala|garam masala]]\n*¼ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric]] powder\n*1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] paste\n*1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]] paste\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n*[[Cookbook:Cilantro|Cilantro]], for garnishing\n\n==Procedure==\n# [[Cookbook:Soaking Beans|Soak]] the chickpeas overnight in water.\n# [[Cookbook:Pressure Cooking|Pressure cook]] the chickpeas until done (3 whistles).\n# Heat the cooking oil in a pot. Add the onions and [[Cookbook:Sautéing|sauté]] until golden brown.\n# Add the turmeric powder, chilli powder, garam masala, and Madras curry powder.\n# Add the tomatoes, ginger, and garlic paste and stir for about 1 minute.\n# Add the boiled chickpeas and some water.\n# Add salt to taste. Cook for about 10 minutes on medium heat.\n# [[Cookbook:Garnish|Garnish]] with cilantro and serve with chapattis or paratha.\n\n== See also ==\n\n* [[Cookbook:Cholley|Cholley]]\n\n[[Category:Recipes for curry|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chickpea]]\n[[Category:Indian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes for stew|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Gluten-free recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Low-GI recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cilantro]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garam masala]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic paste]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ginger paste]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Chickpea Curry (Masaledaar Chole)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-li